technical expertise needed to teach users how to secure their systems. (See section 10.2);

• Physical and Environmental. Support and operations staff often control the immediate
physical area around the system. (See section 10.11);

• Technical Controls. The technical controls are installed, maintained, and used by support
and operations staff.

Organizations: (i) periodically assess the security controls in organizational systems to determine
if the controls are effective in their application; (ii) develop and implement plans of action
designed to correct deficiencies and reduce or eliminate vulnerabilities in organizational systems;
(iii) authorize the operation of organizational systems and any associated system connections;
and (iv) monitor security controls on an ongoing basis to ensure the continued effectiveness of
the controls.

Organizations: (i) identify, report, and correct information and system flaws in a timely manner;
(ii) provide protection from malicious code at appropriate locations within organizational
systems; and (iii) monitor system security alerts and advisories and respond appropriately.
